# Shell scripts must keep LF endings wherever they are checked out or archived.
#
# The container entrypoints (scripts/start-web.sh, scripts/run-refresh.sh) run
# under bash in a Linux image. With core.autocrlf=true on a Windows clone,
# `git archive` emits CRLF, and `set -euo pipefail\r` then fails at boot with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name" — the container restart-loops. The
# committed blobs are already LF; this pins the checkout and archive side too.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
